<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Kawagoe Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1545–1546</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Kawagoe, Night Battle of Kawagoe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of Kawagoe Castle was a battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> in which the Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-clan">Hojo clan</a> defended Kawagoe Castle in Musashi province against a large coalition of the Uesugi clans and the Ashikaga of Koga. In 1546 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-ujiyasu">Hojo Ujiyasu</a> relieved the castle with a surprise night attack that routed the besiegers. The victory made the Hojo the leading power in the Kanto.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-kawagoe-castle.jpg" alt="Siege of Kawagoe Castle" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ocdp · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kawagoejou.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
